// A float literal past the largest finite value of the type it lands in is
// LIT002, never a silent infinity (PROP-021 §2.9, slice 21F). Expected,
// worked by hand: `f32` is the 32-bit IEEE format (23 fraction bits, bias
// 127), whose largest finite value is (2 - 2^-23) * 2^127, about
// 3.4028235e38; 1e39 is past it, and past the halfway point to 2^128
// (about 3.4028236e38), so it would round to infinity.
fn main() {
    let x: f32 = 1e39;
    print(x);
}
